{
  "method": "40 explicitly selected text controls across all 16 original native PNGs. Read RGB pixels without resizing or changing images. For each capture metadata rectangle inset by 2 pixels, choose the actual pixel nearest the source palette RGB by squared Euclidean distance (row-major tie). This targets a glyph core, not antialias edges. Select a visually blank 5x5 local background patch; retain the actual background pixel yielding the lowest WCAG sRGB relative-luminance contrast ratio with that core pixel. This produces 40 final actual-pixel pairs, not exhaustive text/edge/texture coverage. 4 disabled controls are reported separately; no WCAG conformance claim. For frame 14 primary caption, the foreground ROI is additionally restricted to central 30–90% width to exclude the brighter numeric shortcut. At compact scale the nearest-to-source glyph core can itself remain coverage blended; these measured rendered pixels are retained, not replaced with source RGB. Outer antialias fringe pixels are not measured.",
